<%# The game grid. Locals: games (enumerable of Game), focus_slug (String or nil).

    Rendered BOTH on first load and by every Nfl::LiveBroadcast update, from
    the same partial with the same locals — that identity is what stops a
    broadcast-replaced board from drifting away from a freshly loaded one.

    EVERY CARD IS A BUTTON, and the game currently in the focus panel is not
    drawn here at all. `focus` is Alpine state declared on the page wrapper,
    OUTSIDE this target: a broadcast replaces this whole partial on every score,
    so state declared in here would be reset by the next touchdown and the
    reader's chosen game would silently jump back to the server's pick
    mid-play. Declared out there, it survives every replacement and the fresh
    cards read it as Alpine initialises them.

    The inline `display:none` on the focused card is the same first-paint guard
    the focus panel uses: Alpine boots after first paint, so without it the
    board opens with the focused game drawn twice for a frame. %>
<% focus_slug = local_assigns.fetch(:focus_slug, nil) %>
<% ordered = games.sort_by { |g| [g.live? ? 0 : (g.completed? ? 2 : 1), g.kickoff_at || Time.current] } %>
<% if ordered.empty? %>
  <div class="card p-8 text-center">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">No games on the board yet.</p>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">The score poller fills this in as games are scheduled.</p>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <%# One across on a phone, TWO on a tablet, FOUR on a desktop. The jump to
      four waits for xl (1280px) rather than lg: at 1024 a four-up row leaves
      each card about 250px, which starts truncating the longer city names
      ("San Francisco", "New England"). %>
  <div class="grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
    <% ordered.each do |game| %>
      <%# A BUTTON WRAPPING THE CARD, matching contests/_live_game_chip rather
          than inventing a second way to make a game tile clickable. The tile
          itself is untouched — it is shared with the focus panel and with the
          contest page, and a partial that renders differently depending on who
          is listening is how two boards drift apart. %>
      <button type="button"
              data-test="live-grid-card"
              data-pick-slug="<%= game.slug %>"
              x-show="focus !== '<%= game.slug %>'"
              style="<%= "display: none" if game.slug == focus_slug %>"
              @click="select('<%= game.slug %>')"
              class="block w-full text-left cursor-pointer transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 motion-reduce:transform-none">
        <%# The tile already names the teams and reads out the score, so it
            names this button; this says what pressing it DOES, which nothing
            visible has to. %>
        <span class="sr-only">Focus this game.</span>
        <%= render "live/game_tile", game: game %>
      </button>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
